Rule 6 (tuple of axes: indices are unique even after negative-index normalization)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : i = j ∨ (v_2[i] ≠ v_2[j] ∧ v_2[i] + ndim(v_1) ≠ v_2[j] ∧ v_2[j] + ndim(v_1) ≠ v_2[i])
